        "comments": "The assembly daSolVirg1.hap1.1 is based on 40x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 2 (43,833 ? 50,287 Kbp). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 5 (46,529 ? 61,887 Kbp). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 9 (51,790 ? 59,207 Kbp).\nThe exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 7 (37,282 ? 38,295 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 8 (18,788 ? 20,846 Kbp) are unknown.",
